---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { u } from '../lib/games.mjs';

const title = 'About ClassPlay — Screened Classroom Games';
const description = 'ClassPlay is a carefully screened shelf of free browser games for school: math, puzzles, logic, gentle skill games and sports. No downloads, no accounts.';
const canonical = 'https://classplay.online/about/';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <div class="crumbs">
    <a href={u()}>Home</a> › About ClassPlay
  </div>

  <article class="prose" style="margin-top: 16px;">
    <h1>About ClassPlay</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      ClassPlay is a curated catalog of free browser games screened specifically for the classroom,
      school Chromebooks, and student break times.
    </p>

    <h2>Screened for the Classroom First</h2>
    <p>
      Most gaming websites serve anything they can find. ClassPlay is built with the opposite approach:
      we start from what belongs in a school environment. Every game in our catalog is screened for content
      and tone. You will find math puzzles, logic challenges, gentle arcade games, and two-player sports
      that students can share on a single keyboard — but zero shooters, zero horror, zero zombie games,
      and zero violent imagery. If a title would make a teacher or parent frown, it does not get listed.
    </p>

    <h2>Built for School Chromebooks &amp; Modern Browsers</h2>
    <p>
      Schools rely heavily on Chromebooks and managed devices. ClassPlay games run directly in modern web
      browsers as lightweight HTML5 applications. There are no downloads, no installations, no browser
      extensions, and no accounts required. Games load in seconds and fit neatly into a class break or
      reward time.
    </p>

    <h2>Licensed Feeds &amp; Content Partners</h2>
    <p>
      Games on ClassPlay are sourced through licensed web game distribution networks, primarily GameDistribution
      and GameMonetize, and remain the intellectual property of their talented independent developers.
      We screen the upstream feeds to select only titles that meet our classroom standards.
    </p>

    <h2>Regular Reviews &amp; Safety Maintenance</h2>
    <p>
      We review our catalog continuously. Games that change content, slow down, or introduce intrusive
      elements are promptly pruned. Teachers and parents with questions or suggestions are encouraged to
      <a href={u('contact/')}>reach out to us</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
